# Fly.io deployment (2026-09-20). Both `cargo build` (Dockerfile's `rust`
# stage) and `pnpm build` (its `web` stage) need the whole repository as
# their build context -- collect-maps.mjs falls back to ../data and Vite's
# @bindings alias resolves ../bindings, both outside web/ -- so this file
# is what keeps that context from also dragging in everything that never
# needs to leave the host.

# Build output and local dev state -- regenerated inside the image, never
# reused from the host; a stale local build here must never leak in.
target/
web/dist/
web/node_modules/
node_modules/
.maps/
web/public/maps/

# VCS metadata -- irrelevant to any stage and large in a repo with any history.
.git/
.gitignore

# The frozen reference implementation (CLAUDE.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md):
# "not the product codebase," and no Dockerfile stage imports or shells
# out to it. Excluded so it can't be mistaken for something the image
# depends on, not because it would be expensive to include.
src/tolmap/
viewer/
eval/
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Locally-built native libs from a host run of scripts/install-leiden.sh
# (defaults to $PWD/.native/leiden) -- the `native` stage builds its own
# copy inside the image; a host copy must never be substituted for it.
.native/

# Editor/OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
